🚀 Git Commands — Complete Step-by-Step Guide
Bhai, ab main tujhe har command step-by-step batata hoon jo tu CMD / PowerShell / Git Bash me chalayega. Ye commands tere current repo (vishakha2121/enterprise-simulation-engine) ke liye ready hain.

📌 STEP 0: Pehle Ye Check Kar
CMD khol aur ye chala:

bash
git --version
Agar version dikha (jaise git version 2.42.0) → ✅ aage badh

Agar not recognized aaya → Git install kar: https://git-scm.com/download/win

📌 STEP 1: Apne Project Folder Me Jao
CMD me apne project folder tak navigate kar. Example:

bash
cd C:\Users\YourName\Desktop\enterprise-simulation-engine
Verify kar ki sahi folder me hai:

bash
dir
Ye teri files dikhayega (README.md, backend, frontend, etc.)

📌 STEP 2: Git Initialize Karo (Sirf Pehli Baar)
Agar folder me .git folder nahi hai toh ye chala:

bash
git init
Check kar ki Git initialized hai:

bash
git status
Output me On branch main ya On branch master dikhega.

📌 STEP 3: Git Config Setup (Sirf Pehli Baar)
Apna naam aur email set kar (jo GitHub pe hai):

bash
git config --global user.name "Vishakha"
git config --global user.email "your-email@gmail.com"
⚠️ your-email@gmail.com apne actual GitHub email se replace kar dena.

Verify:

bash
git config --global --list
📌 STEP 4: Files Add Karo (Staging)
bash
git add .
. ka matlab hai — saari files aur folders add karo.

Verify ki kya add hua:

bash
git status
Sab files green me dikhni chahiye (staged files).

📌 STEP 5: Commit Karo
bash
git commit -m "Initial commit: Enterprise Simulation Engine setup"
Agar ye error aaya — Please tell me who you are → Step 3 dobara kar.

📌 STEP 6: Branch Name Set Karo
bash
git branch -M main
📌 STEP 7: Remote Add Karo (Sirf Pehli Baar)
bash
git remote add origin https://github.com/vishakha2121/enterprise-simulation-engine.git
Agar remote origin already exists error aaya toh pehle remove kar:

bash
git remote remove origin
git remote add origin https://github.com/vishakha2121/enterprise-simulation-engine.git
Verify:

bash
git remote -v
Output me GitHub URL dikhna chahiye.

📌 STEP 8: Push Karo 🚀
bash
git push -u origin main
