🏗️ Architecture
text
┌─────────────┐      ┌──────────────┐      ┌─────────────┐
│   React     │─────▶│   FastAPI    │─────▶│   SQLite    │
│  Frontend   │◀─────│   Backend    │◀─────│     DB      │
└─────────────┘      └──────┬───────┘      └─────────────┘
                            │
                     ┌──────┴───────┐
                     │              │
              ┌──────▼─────┐  ┌────▼──────┐
              │ Monte Carlo│  │  Gemini   │
              │   + RL     │  │    API    │
              └────────────┘  └───────────┘
Data Flow
User submits scenario (form or natural language)

Gemini API parses natural language → structured parameters

Simulation Engine runs Monte Carlo (10,000 iterations) + RL agent

Results stored in SQLite + returned as JSON

React Dashboard renders charts, insights, and recommendations

Detailed architecture → docs/architecture.md

📚 API Reference
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/v1/simulation/run	Run a Monte Carlo simulation
POST	/api/v1/simulation/rl	Train RL agent for a scenario
POST	/api/v1/chat/message	Send message to Gemini chat
GET	/api/v1/history	Get all past simulations
GET	/api/v1/history/{id}	Get specific simulation
DELETE	/api/v1/history/{id}	Delete a simulation
GET	/api/v1/health	Health check endpoint
Full interactive API docs → http://localhost:8000/docs (Swagger UI auto-generated by FastAPI)

🎓 How It Works
🔵 Monte Carlo Flow
User provides parameters: price, cost, demand_mean, demand_std

Engine samples 10,000 random demand values from a normal distribution

For each sample → calculate: profit = (price - cost) × demand

Aggregate results → mean, std deviation, percentiles (P5, P50, P95), histogram

Return profit distribution + confidence intervals

🟢 Reinforcement Learning Flow
Define state space: {inventory, cash, market_share}

Define action space: {increase_price, decrease_price, hire, invest}

Reward = profit delta at each step

Q-Learning updates Q-table over N episodes (ε-greedy exploration)

Extract optimal policy → recommend best actions per state

🟣 Gemini Flow
User types: "Simulate pricing with cost 60, price 100, demand around 1000"

Gemini extracts structured JSON:

json
{
  "scenario": "pricing",
  "params": { "cost": 60, "price": 100, "demand_mean": 1000, "demand_std": 200 }
}
Backend routes to correct simulation module

Returns structured results + natural language explanation

